 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No motif on the Prophet ﷺ; their plot (30:6-10) is not glossed in detail. Their claims (31) and their prayer for punishment (32) are framed («جهلا منهم وعنادًا», «على وجه الجزم منهم بباطلهم»). «ويمكر الله» carries Al-Muyassar's «وردَّ الله مكرهم عليهم». Light for «إن تتقوا الله». STAGING v4: c1 (29) stays ambient: a conditional promise of Allah's acts (criterion, expiation, forgiveness) and His bounty. c2 (30-32): two small groups of polytheists (three each) facing one another in a town by day, the second walking in to join the first (Al-Muyassar: in Mecca; As-Sa'di: their council in Dar an-Nadwa); they speak to each other on 30:2 and 30:11 (their plotting); the three options of 30:6-10 get camera only, no gesture; the Prophet is never drawn and the address to him (30:3) gets no beat. A geometric plate for Allah's plan (30:12-31:1). 31: a book plate for the verses recited to them (31:2); they speak (31:5, 31:8) and shake their heads on 31:13 (their claim, framed by Al-Muyassar's gloss). 32: they speak on 32:2, 32:11 and 32:17 (their challenge); no stones, no sky shot and no darkness: nothing they asked for is shown as happening. The two groups always face one another (their speech marks point at each other), never an empty side; the left of the stage is empty and nobody faces it."
 },
